olidation more than expected.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Daniel Webster (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Daniel Webster's retirement leaves this Central Florida seat open, but the district's R+7 lean and a Republican-friendly environment keep it firmly in the GOP column. Joe Strada, an HVAC businessman who survived a recount to win his primary, has raised $5.5 million with outside backing, while Democrat James Pericola has raised about $226,000. A Libertarian candidate is also on the ballot.\n\nRaters across the spectrum call the race Safe R or Likely R, and prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a one-in-ten chance. A July poll showed a tie, but it is dated and Democratic-sponsored, so the forecast relies on fundamentals and points to a comfortable Republican win of about eleven points.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1071, "margin": -7.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1312, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1199, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0703, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0839, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0989, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1239, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0883, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1092, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0593, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1139, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1139, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.126, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1066, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.079, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0406, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0761, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0527, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0